          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden class="text-ink-300">·</span><span>Similarity search becomes an implicit governance layer.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden class="text-ink-300">·</span><span>Output quality depends on retrieval luck and prompt phrasing.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-lg border border-ink-100 bg-paper-muted p-6 text-ink-500 transition-colors">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Data structure approach</p>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-ink-900">GraphRAG</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden class="text-ink-300">·</span><span>Knowledge is organized as entities and relationships rather than only flat chunks.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden class="text-ink-300">·</span><span>Strong for multi-hop reasoning across people, systems, documents, and dependencies.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden class="text-ink-300">·</span><span>Useful when the problem depends on traversing a connected knowledge structure.</span></li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden class="text-ink-300">·</span><span>Requires graph construction and maintenance before retrieval can work well.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

